  "goodToKnow": "Der Volksvertreter (die Volksvertreterin) is an elected representative of the people, a slightly elevated word for der Abgeordnete. Parliament is the Volksvertretung. According to Article 38 of the Grundgesetz, members of the Bundestag are representatives of the whole people, not bound by orders, and subject only to their conscience. The plural is the same: die Volksvertreter."
